# Dependencies and build output (this project has no build step; kept in case
# a toolchain is added later)
node_modules/
dist/
# `spike/` was ignored here on the assumption these pages get deleted once they
# have answered their question. That assumption was wrong twice over, and the
# second correction removed the directory: ⑤ and ⑥ were each reopened by a
# later finding, and then it turned out that EVERY answer they hold — CPU,
# battery, AEC, transcription quality — is an answer about one phone in one
# room, and expires when either changes. The apparatus had to stay; what it
# did not have to be was a second copy of the engines. It lives in
# web/audio-bench.html now, driving phone/audio/'s own modules, which is what
# makes a reading worth taking back to them.

# Connectivity-test fixture audio: each person's own voice, recorded locally
# per core/fixtures/README.md, never someone else's sample.
core/fixtures/*.wav
# Except these. They are synthesised, so they are nobody's voice, and every
# clone hears the same take — which is what lets the setup sheet ask "is this
# layer reachable" without asking anyone to record anything first. They cannot
# answer "does it understand *me*"; that is what the recorded three are for.
# There are two because an English-only user tested against a code-switching
# clip fails a setup that works perfectly well for them.
!core/fixtures/check-*.wav

# Personal design notes and specs (Chinese, single-author working documents)
docs/design-notes/
docs/superpowers/

# OS and editors
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.superpowers/

# Brain-server models: downloaded by server/models/fetch.sh, 6 MB, not vendored
# because nothing here needs a source build.
server/models/*
!server/models/fetch.sh

# Built by npm start (or npm run admin:build); never committed.
admin/dist/

# Cloudflare wrangler local cache
.wrangler/

# ESP32 firmware build output (idf.py, and the host tests' CMake tree).
# dependencies.lock is committed.
firmware/build/
firmware/build-host/
firmware/sdkconfig
firmware/sdkconfig.old
firmware/managed_components/
